<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Elasticsearch on MCP Toolbox for Databases</title><link>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/elasticsearch/</link><description>Recent content in Elasticsearch on MCP Toolbox for Databases</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/elasticsearch/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Elasticsearch Source</title><link>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/elasticsearch/source/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/elasticsearch/source/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="about"&gt;About&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/index.html"&gt;Elasticsearch&lt;/a&gt; is a distributed, free and open search and&#10;analytics engine for all types of data, including textual, numerical,&#10;geospatial, structured, and unstructured.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If you are new to Elasticsearch, you can learn how to&#10;&lt;a href="https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/getting-started.html"&gt;set up a cluster and start indexing data&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Elasticsearch uses &lt;a href="https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/esql.html"&gt;ES|QL&lt;/a&gt; for querying data. ES|QL&#10;is a powerful query language that allows you to search and aggregate data in&#10;Elasticsearch.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;See the &lt;a href="https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/index.html"&gt;official&#10;documentation&lt;/a&gt;&#10;for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="available-tools"&gt;Available Tools&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Elasticsearch Source Tools&lt;/h3&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;table&gt;&#10; &lt;thead&gt;&#10; &lt;tr&gt;&#10; &lt;th&gt;Tool Name&lt;/th&gt;&#10; &lt;th&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;&#10; &lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &lt;/thead&gt;&#10; &lt;tbody&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;tr&gt;&#10; &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/elasticsearch/tools/elasticsearch-esql/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;elasticsearch-esql&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10; &lt;td&gt;Execute ES|QL queries.&#10;&lt;/td&gt;&#10; &lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;tr&gt;&#10; &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/elasticsearch/tools/elasticsearch-execute-esql/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;elasticsearch-execute-esql&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10; &lt;td&gt;Execute arbitrary ES|QL statements.&#10;&lt;/td&gt;&#10; &lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;/tbody&gt;&#10; &lt;/table&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="requirements"&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="api-key"&gt;API Key&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Toolbox uses an &lt;a href="https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/security-api-create-api-key.html"&gt;API key&lt;/a&gt; to authorize and authenticate when&#10;interacting with &lt;a href="https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/index.html"&gt;Elasticsearch&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>